[statement]
`b` 3, the best candidate for `b`, needs `a`, whose one candidate, `a` 2,
has the condition `b` and needs `w`, which only `b` 2 provides. `b` 3
completes `a` 2's condition, and a package with a condition steers no
choice that completes it
(`install-if/a-package-whose-condition-holds-does-not-steer-the-choice-completing-it`),
though it is a dependency of that choice too: apk takes `b` 3 for `b` and
refuses, as it does where `a` 2 has no condition.

[repository]
P:b
V:2
p:w=3

P:b
V:3
D:a

P:a
V:2
D:w
i:b

[request]
b

